+/* A scope that follows the real sound at the cost of one or two parameter changes per redraw (vst.json "scope").
+ * MPC spends ~1 ms of its screen thread per parameter change it is told about and ~40 ms per "re-read everything"
+ * (measured on a Live II, 2026-10-02), so a scope drawn from many display parameters (one per column) was far too
+ * heavy. Instead the plugin's own output is cut into a window as a scope triggers (scope.h) and matched to the nearest
+ * of SCOPE_K shapes recorded offline from this engine across its settings (steve/tools/scope); the skin holds those
+ * shapes as filmstrips, a bank parameter picks the strip and a frame parameter the shape. Silence shows shape 0, a flat
+ * line. A small hysteresis keeps the picture from flickering between near-equal shapes. Audio thread, after the
+ * block; the host is called without the engine lock held. */
